 "summary": "Not on BTC, ETH and SOL. After price crossed the SAR, or while it stayed above or below it, price moved about the same as after random candles on 1h, 4h and daily. No result holds up: the only pooled one above the luck band, the short after a 1h cross down, rests on signals of Jan 10, 2021 and shows at 20 candles only.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long on a cross up through the SAR",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, with the default settings and with Start 0.01, Increment 0.01."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting a cross down through the SAR",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "Beat random on 1h by 0.07%, the top of the luck band, and only because of signals on Jan 10, 2021. Same as random on 4h and daily."
  },
  {
   "use": "Staying long while price is above the SAR",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. On daily it beat random in uptrends, but one long stretch carries that."
  },
  {
   "use": "Staying short while price is below the SAR",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, pooled across the three pairs."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, price crossing up through the SAR gave 6,687 entries in 4,085 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.06% ahead of random entries, inside a luck band of -0.05% to 0.07%. The same cross lands inside the band on 4h and daily too.",
  "The short after a 1h cross down through the SAR was 0.07% better than random, right at the band's top. Its strongest stretch is 2 entries on Jan 10, 2021, and without it the result is chance. At 10, 50 and 100 candles it is chance as well. On 4h and daily the same short was inside the band.",
  "Trend regime flips two of these results. On 1h, the long cross beat random by 0.08% in downtrends, but only because of signals on Nov 9–10, 2022, during the FTX collapse. In uptrends it was 0.01%, same as random. On 1h the short cross did 0.1% better than random in downtrends and held without Nov 7–8, 2022, but showed at 20 candles only.",
  "On 4h the long cross went the other way. In uptrends it did 0.28% worse than random, resting on 2 entries between May 18, 2021 and May 20, 2021, during the May 2021 crash. In downtrends it was 0.23%, inside the band.",
  "The level conditions enter on almost every candle: on 1h, price above the SAR gave 82,668 entries but only 1,006 separate moves. On daily, staying long above the SAR beat random by 2.02% in uptrends, but 183 entries between Feb 27, 2021 and Jan 18, 2022 carry it. In downtrends it did 1.03% worse, inside the band. Staying short below the SAR on daily shows the same shape: 2.59% in uptrends from 49 entries between Nov 10, 2021 and Jan 19, 2022, nothing in downtrends.",
  "A slower SAR, Start 0.01 and Increment 0.01, fires about three fifths as often on 1h as the default and was same as random pooled. On SOL 1h it beat random by 0.24% against a band topping at 0.19%. That held without its strongest entry and at 50 and 100 candles, though not at 10. On BTC and ETH it was inside the band.",
  "For a DCA bot, a PSAR flip as the start condition only sets when deals open. On these pairs it did not change where price went, so the take profit and DCA spacing decide the outcome. The one result worth testing as a filter beside other conditions is the long cross with Start 0.01 on SOL 1h. A short bot that opens on 1h flips leans on single stretches, so leave that setting out or test it on your own pair."
 ],
